      "explanation": "Correct: (B) 3.1 m/s. In one period the child travels one circumference, so v = 2πr/T = 2π(2.0 m)/(4.0 s) = 12.6 m/4.0 s ≈ 3.1 m/s. The frequency is f = 1/T = 0.25 Hz, which gives the same result through v = 2πrf. The clue is \"one revolution every 4.0 s,\" which is the period of the uniform circular motion, so the distance per revolution must be the full circumference 2πr.\n\n(A) is wrong because 0.50 m/s divides the radius by the period (2.0/4.0) and leaves out the factor of 2π, so it is not the distance traveled per revolution.\n(C) is wrong because 6.3 m/s uses the diameter, 4.0 m, in place of the radius in 2πr, which doubles the distance traveled in one revolution.\n(D) is wrong because 1.6 m/s uses πr, half the circumference, as the distance in one period, so it is exactly half the correct speed.",
