            "Trial 2 after: p_dart = (0.050)(−2.0) = −0.10 kg·m/s = −1 unit (a bar one unit BELOW the zero line); p_cart = 0.40 − (−0.10) = +0.50 kg·m/s = +5 units; system = −1 + 5 = +4 units.",
            "The key visual difference: in Trial 2 the cart's after-bar (5 units) is taller than the system bar, which is possible only because the dart's bar has gone negative."
