            "Torque: τ = rF = (0.020 m)(15 N) = 0.30 N·m.",
            "Work: W = τΔθ = (0.30 N·m)(30 rad) = 9.0 J. (Check: Fs = (15 N)(0.60 m) = 9.0 J.)",
            "With no friction, the string's torque is the only torque, so by the rotational work-energy theorem W_net = ΔK_rot = ½Iω² − 0.",
            "ω = √(2W/I) = √(2(9.0)/0.080) = √225 = 15 rad/s."
